  "rules": [
    "Model exhibits severe upward bias when recent history shows a strong downtrend (e.g., Example 3, 4, 5) despite high volatility spikes; true outcomes often reverse immediately after the model's first few days.",
    "When sentiment history contains mixed signals (positive and negative extremes) within the last 18 days, the model fails to capture the mean-reverting nature of EU ETS prices, consistently overestimating the next 30-day range.",
    "The model displays significant lag in reacting to sudden price spikes; true outcomes often peak within the first 5-7 days while the model's forecast remains flat or slowly rising.",
    "In high-volatility regimes (standard deviation > 2.0), the model should apply a volatility compression correction factor of -15% to its initial forecast to avoid systematic overshoots.",
    "If the last 3 days of history show a downward trend but sentiment is neutral or slightly positive, reduce the model's upward drift by 8-10 EUR over the 30-day horizon."
  ]
